You do not need to call yourself a carer to be one. If you **regularly help someone** who could not manage without you, you have rights and may be able to get support.

## In this guide

- [Carer's Allowance](/support/carers/carers-allowance/): money for people who care for 35 hours a week or more
- [Carers' rights and support](/support/carers/carers-rights/): carer's assessments, carer's leave, flexible working and breaks

## Quick tips

- **Tell your GP** you are a carer. Many surgeries offer flexible appointments, health checks and a free flu vaccine for carers.
- Ask your council for a free **carer's assessment**.
- Many venues give **free carer tickets**. See [days out and leisure](/support/leisure/).
- **Carers UK** runs a free helpline, and local carers' centres offer support and breaks.
